              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Bengali for to warm oneself, then the Bengali for a guide (for visitors)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ঠিকানা",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ঠিকানা — ṭhikānā — \"an address\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "আমি বন্ধুর নতুন ঠিকানা খুঁজে পেলাম। āmi bôndhur nôtun ṭhikānā khũje pelām. I found my friend's new address."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It shares its first syllable with ঠিক, right: an address is the place a thing is fixed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ঠিকানা (ṭhikānā) is inherited: CDIAL lists Bengali ṭhikānā, \"a station, a fixed place\", beside ṭhik, \"correct\", under the reconstructed ṭhīkka, \"firm, right\" (CDIAL 5503); the sense \"a postal address\" is the modern use."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
